**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key Issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| Medium | 1 | Leap-year Feb 29 causes 1-day schedule misalignment in `compute_schedule_offset` — uses wall-clock ordinal without accounting for 365-day schedule length vs 366-day leap years |
| Low | 3 | `ScheduleSource::mean()` vs `annual_mean_fraction()` weighting inconsistency; `TimeWindow` stochastic noise zero-mean convention not enforced; `DailyProfile` lacks holiday support |

**Verified correct:** duty cycle fractions (0.0–1.0), multiplicative month/weekday/weekend/hour combination, half-open interval convention `[t, t+dt)`, midnight wrapping, DST-aware civil-time schedule indexing, and stochastic RNG determinism/reproducibility.
